{"id":"G3850","lemma":"παραβολή","transliteration":"parabolē","sayIt":"parabolē","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, feminine","gloss":"parable","meaning":"παραβολή, -ῆς, ἡ\n(παραβάλλω), [in LXX (cf. McNeile, Mt., 185): Num.23:7, Deu.28:37, Psa.44:14, Pro.1:6, Eze.12:22, al. (מָשַׁל), Sir.47:17 (חִידָה), al. mutt. in Sir, Wis.5:3 ;]\n1. a placing beside, juxtaposition (Polyb., al.).\n2. a comparing, comparison (Plat., Arist., al.).\n3. a comparison, illustration, analogy, figure (Arist., al.) : Mat.24:32, Mrk.3:23, Heb.9:9 11:19; specif. of the pictures and narratives drawn from nature and human life which are characteristic of the synoptic teaching of our Lord, a parable: Mat.13:3, 10 Mrk.4:2, 10, Luk.8:4, 9-11, al.; with genitive ref., Mat.13:18, 36\n4 4 Like Heb. מָשַׁל (1Ki.10:12, Pro.1:6, Sir.3:29, al.), = παροιμία, a proverb or gnomic saying: Luk.4:23 5:36 6:39\nSYN.: παροιμία (see Abbott, Essays, 82 ff.) (AS)","glosses":["parable","parables","lesson","proverb","illustration","sense"],"count":48,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"parables","kjv":"parables"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"parables"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":13,"renderings":{"bsb":"parables","kjv":"parables"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":18,"renderings":{"bsb":"parable","kjv":"the parable"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":24,"renderings":{"bsb":"parable","kjv":"parable"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":31,"renderings":{"bsb":"parable","kjv":"parable"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":33,"renderings":{"bsb":"parable","kjv":"parable"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":34,"renderings":{"bsb":"parables","kjv":"parables"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":35,"renderings":{"bsb":"parables","kjv":"parables"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":36,"renderings":{"bsb":"parable","kjv":"the parable"}},{"chapterId":"mat-13","v":53,"renderings":{"bsb":"parables","kjv":"parables"}},{"chapterId":"mat-15","v":15,"renderings":{"bsb":"parable"}},{"chapterId":"mat-21","v":33,"renderings":{"bsb":"par